---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Calileus | Software Architect">
  <header class="site-header">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 flex items-center justify-between h-20">
      <a href="#top" class="brand-mark" aria-label="Calileus home">
        <span class="brand-mark__dot"></span>
        <span>Calileus<span class="text-brand-400">.</span></span>
      </a>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
        <nav class="hidden md:flex items-center gap-7 text-sm text-surface-400" aria-label="Main navigation">
          <a href="#impact" class="nav-link">Impact</a>
          <a href="#expertise" class="nav-link">Expertise</a>
          <a href="#experience" class="nav-link">Experience</a>
          <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/calileus" class="nav-cta">Let's talk <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </nav>
        <button type="button" class="theme-toggle" data-theme-toggle aria-label="Toggle light and dark theme" aria-pressed="false">
          <span class="theme-toggle__icon" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="theme-toggle__glyph theme-toggle__glyph--sun">☀</span>
            <span class="theme-toggle__glyph theme-toggle__glyph--moon">☾</span>
          </span>
          <span class="hidden md:inline" data-theme-label>Dark</span>
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main id="top">
    <section class="hero-section max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6" aria-labelledby="hero-heading">
      <div class="hero-grid-pattern" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot"></span> Software Architect</p>
        <h1 id="hero-heading">Building <span class="gradient-text">dependable software</span></h1>
        <p class="hero-lede">I turn complex product requirements into production-ready software.</p>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 items-center mt-9">
          <a href="#experience" class="btn-primary">Explore my work <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
          <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/calileus" class="btn-secondary">Get in touch <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-meta"><span class="meta-divider"></span><span>M.Sc. Mathematics · Querétaro, Mexico</span><span class="meta-divider"></span></div>
      </div>
      <aside class="hero-visual" aria-label="Calileus engineering identity">
        <div class="hero-visual__frame">
          <img src={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/profile.jpg`} alt="Calileus illustrated engineering identity" />
          <div class="hero-visual__scanline" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <div class="hero-visual__label hero-visual__label--top">CALILEUS LAB</div>
          <div class="hero-visual__label hero-visual__label--bottom"><span class="status-dot"></span> ARCHITECTING a STABLE FUTURE</div>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-visual__caption"><span>Personal identity:</span><strong>Code · Honor · Legacy</strong></div>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <section id="impact" class="section-band max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6" aria-labelledby="impact-heading">
      <div class="section-intro"><p class="eyebrow">01 / OUTCOMES</p><h2 id="impact-heading">Engineering judgment, measured.</h2><p>Senior engineering is making the right tradeoffs visible. These are the outcomes I use to evaluate whether a system and a team are getting better.</p></div>
      <div class="impact-grid">
        <div class="impact-item impact-item--featured"><strong>60<span>%</span></strong><span>review effort reduction via 10+ GitHub Actions workflows deployed across 8 components, adopted by 25+ contributors</span></div>
        <div class="impact-item"><strong>58<span>+</span></strong><span>releases delivered; 12 customer-facing releases supporting North American production programs</span></div>
        <div class="impact-item"><strong>99<span>%</span></strong><span>first-pass execution success (improved from 20%); integration reliability and deployment consistency</span></div>
        <div class="impact-item"><strong>80<span>%</span></strong><span>package reduction after modernizing legacy monolithic codebase into modular architecture</span></div>
        <div class="impact-item"><strong>14</strong><span>multidisciplinary engineers led through quotation, planning, implementation, validation, and deployment</span></div>
        <div class="impact-item"><strong>2,538</strong><span>commits · 280+ code reviews · 240+ merged PRs as primary repository maintainer</span></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="expertise" class="section-band max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6" aria-labelledby="expertise-heading">
      <div class="section-intro"><p class="eyebrow">02 / CAPABILITIES</p><h2 id="expertise-heading">From architecture intent to working software.</h2><p>A pragmatic technical range grounded in modern C++, quality engineering, and the operating systems that make delivery repeatable.</p></div>
      <div class="capability-grid">
        <article class="capability-card"><span class="capability-number">01</span><h3>Architecture & design</h3><p>Component boundaries, event-driven systems, object processing pipelines, API design, and cross-platform decomposition. Automotive systems: safety-critical software, MISRA compliance, sensor fusion patterns.</p><div class="tag-row"><span>C++20</span><span>Distributed systems</span><span>Protobuf</span><span>Safety-critical</span></div></article>
        <article class="capability-card"><span class="capability-number">02</span><h3>Quality as a system</h3><p>MISRA C/C++, static analysis, review standards, test strategy, and automated gates that protect engineering focus. Enforcement mechanisms that scale from 5 to 50+ engineers.</p><div class="tag-row"><span>GoogleTest</span><span>clang-format</span><span>CI quality gates</span><span>Code review discipline</span></div></article>
        <article class="capability-card"><span class="capability-number">03</span><h3>Delivery leadership</h3><p>Repository governance, release models, technical direction, mentoring, and the communication between product and engineering. Cross-platform (Linux/Windows) deployment, customer integration workflows.</p><div class="tag-row"><span>GitHub Actions</span><span>CMake</span><span>Linux / Windows</span><span>Team mentoring</span></div></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-band max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6" aria-labelledby="philosophy-heading">
      <div class="section-intro"><p class="eyebrow">02.5 / PHILOSOPHY</p><h2 id="philosophy-heading">How I approach software architecture.</h2></div>
      <div class="philosophy-panel">
        <p>Dependable software isn't built by individuals—it's built by <strong>systems</strong>. Every architecture I design optimizes for three principles:</p>
        <ul class="philosophy-list">
          <li><strong>Clarity</strong> — A system is only as good as the next engineer's ability to understand and modify it. Explicit design decisions, minimal coupling, and living documentation matter more than clever code.</li>
          <li><strong>Testability</strong> — Architecture shapes testability. I design components with clear boundaries, single responsibilities, that can be tested in isolation. This is how quality scales from 5 engineers to 50.</li>
          <li><strong>Team Scalability</strong> — The most important metric: does this architecture make it easier or harder for my team to deliver? Automated quality gates, consistent review standards, and clear governance reduce friction.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>In automotive systems—where dependability means safety for millions of vehicles—these principles aren't optional. MISRA compliance, formal methods, and review discipline are how you build systems that compound in quality over time.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-band max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6" aria-labelledby="certs-heading">
      <div class="section-intro"><p class="eyebrow">02.75 / CONTINUOUS LEARNING</p><h2 id="certs-heading">Staying current with emerging domains.</h2><p>I invest in certifications and skills that shape the future of automotive systems and distributed software.</p></div>
      <div class="certs-grid">
        <div class="cert-card">
          <div class="cert-year">2026</div>
          <h3>Google AI Essentials</h3>
          <p class="cert-issuer">Google</p>
